{
  "_comment": [
    "Labelled eval cases against docs.sample/. sources are matched on basename so the",
    "same case works whether the index was built on the host or inside the container.",
    "must_retrieve: the router is expected to offer answer_docs for this question.",
    "must_abstain: answer_docs is expected to say it does not know.",
    "must_cite: the answer must carry [n] citations that resolve to sources.",
    "",
    "Every 'sources' entry names a file that exists. The corpus is 21 documents across",
    "markdown, csv, json, python, text and pdf, so retrieval is measured rather than",
    "scored against a single 65-byte file.",
    "",
    "'cases' is the TUNING set - it may be tuned against, so its score is optimistic.",
    "'holdout' is written afterwards and never tuned against; that is the honest number,",
    "and it is what the exit code gates on.",
    "",
    "The holdout has been rewritten TWICE, and both times for the same reason. The first",
    "one revealed that the router was answering 'no' to nine document questions; the",
    "second was retired because the eval run that exposed a broken router prompt also",
    "showed its score, so it could no longer be an untouched set. The current set has",
    "never been run against a tuned system. It is not decoration - retire a holdout the",
    "moment you look at its per-case results.",    "",
    "h-nhs and h-bp are near-miss negatives: a relevant document exists, so the router",
    "must still route, but the answer is not in it. They must abstain.",
    "",
    "car-excess is in the tuning set because it FAILS: insurance.md scores 0.491 at",
    "rank 4 against 0.517 for bike-maintenance.md, and the whole top-12 sits inside",
    "0.06. Tuning material by definition - it was measured while building the corpus."
  ],
